    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <Faq />
    <h2 id="install">Install and uninstall</h2>
    <p>Installers are still in testing, so there is nothing to install yet. When a version passes testing on real machines it will be listed in the download section with its checksum, and this page will give step-by-step instructions for Windows and Mac.</p>
    <h2>Reading the numbers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Size on disk</strong> is the space files actually occupy, which is what you get back when you remove them.</li>
      <li><strong>File size</strong> is the amount of data they contain. Compressed, sparse and online-only files can be much smaller on disk.</li>
      <li><strong>Estimated</strong> means Windows did not report the exact figure, so Tessera calculated it from the drive's allocation size.</li>
      <li><strong>Not attributed to scanned files</strong> is space the drive reports as used that belongs to the system, other accounts or folders Tessera was not allowed to read.</li>
    </ul>
  </Prose>
</Base>
